OL,3,AIsrael's far right find fertile ground
OL,4,Aamong first-time voters
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Israel's far-right National
OL,7,FSecurity Minister, Itamar Ben-Gvir,
OL,8,Freached voting age, he was rejected
OL,9,Ffrom Israel's army for being too
OL,10,Fpolitically extreme.
OL,12,FHis views have not changed much in the
OL,13,F30 years since then - but Israel has.
OL,14,FOnce shunned by the political
OL,15,Festablishment, he is now part of the
OL,16,Fgovernment's inner sanctum of
OL,17,Fministers.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
